      "content": "I understand your need for a strictly professional and technical analysis for your risk assessment report. I will provide a detailed breakdown of the thermal risks and fire suppression challenges associated with high-density racking and flammable solvents, adhering to your request for a formal tone without the previous goblin analogies.\n\n### Technical Analysis: Thermal Runaway and Fire Suppression in High-Density Racking\n\n#### 1. Heat Transfer Issues and Thermal Runaway Risks\nThe primary mechanism for thermal runaway in this context is the accumulation of heat and vapor within confined spaces, exacerbated by the geometry of high-density racking.\n\n*   **Restricted Airflow and Heat Dissipation:** High-density racking systems are designed to maximize storage density by minimizing aisle width and utilizing cantilever or narrow-aisle configurations. This significantly reduces natural convection currents. In the event of a solvent leak or a localized exothermic reaction (such as a spontaneous decomposition or friction from a pump), the lack of airflow prevents the dissipation of heat. The heat remains trapped within the rack structure and the immediate vicinity of the affected bottles.\n*   **Vapor Stratification and Ignition:** Flammable solvents have low flash points. In a high-density environment",
